# Everything is kept out of the build context except what cargo reads. The step that
# compiles is cached for as long as these files stay the same, so a change to the
# manifests in deploy/ or to the documentation compiles nothing again; and neither the
# local world nor the target directory is sent to Docker.
#
# Every workspace member has to be let through, including tools/datagen, which is not
# built for the image: cargo does not load a workspace with a member missing. If the
# workspace ever gets members in another top-level directory, add it here.
*
!.cargo
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!bin
!crates
!services
!tools
